       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6400 mg/day, which is double the maximum daily dose on the label (3200 mg/day). A single 1600 mg dose is also above the usual single-dose maximum of 800 mg. Ibuprofen has GI bleeding, renal, and cardiovascular risks, and those rise with dose, so this looks like it could be a dosing error.\n\nThe most common labeled regimen at the maximum is **800 mg by mouth four times daily** (3200 mg/day). A lower dose, such as 400\u2013600 mg every 6 hours, may be appropriate depending on the indication.\n\nPlease confirm one of the following, and I'll enter it:\n1. **800 mg PO QID** (3200 mg/day, the labeled maximum)\n2. A different dose, if 1600 mg per dose is intended. Please confirm the indication and that this is deliberate."
